OL,3,GNEWSAHope for 'productive day' as
OL,4,Abudget talks continue
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe Secretary of State Sir Chris Bryant
OL,7,Fis hosting further talks with the four
OL,8,FNorthern Ireland Executive parties in a
OL,9,Fbid to break Stormont's budget
OL,10,Fdeadlock.
OL,12,FDelegations from Sinn Fein, the
OL,13,FDemocratic Unionist Party (DUP) and the
OL,14,FUlster Unionist Party (UUP) arrived
OL,15,Fseparately at Hillsborough Castle.
OL,17,FSinn Fein President Mary Lou McDonald
OL,18,Fsaid she hoped for a "productive day"
OL,19,Fwhile the UUP leader Jon Burrows said
OL,20,Fhis party was in "deal mode".
OL,23,APub: 05-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
